<title>USA: U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights--USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. soybean major sales activity in the week ended Sept 12 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:  1996/97		     1997/98</p>
<p>Holland	97,300			   Nil</p>
<p>Mexico	 70,800</p>
<p>Japan	  65,900</p>
<p>Germany	64,000</p>
<p>Unknown     -73,000</p>
<p>Net sales of 302,900 tonnes were up 9 percent from the previous week.</p>
<p>Exports of 225,800 tonnes were off 43 percent from the previous week and one-third below the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary export destinations: Japan, Holland, Germany, Mexico and Taiwan.</p>
</text>
